The two rectangles are similar.
What is the area of the larger rectangle?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (1.0,0.7);
\node[above] at (0.5,0.7) {$4\text{ cm}$};
\node[font=\small] at (0.5,0.35) {$5\text{ cm}^2$};
\draw (2.2,0) rectangle (5.2,2.1);
\node[above] at (3.7,2.1) {$12\text{ cm}$};
\node at (3.7,1.05) {$?$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

These two prisms are similar.
Find the volume of the larger prism.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.9]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (1,0);
\coordinate (C) at (1,1);
\coordinate (D) at (0,1);
\coordinate (E) at ($(A)+(30:0.5)$);
\coordinate (F) at ($(B)+(30:0.5)$);
\coordinate (G) at ($(C)+(30:0.5)$);
\coordinate (H) at ($(D)+(30:0.5)$);
\draw (A)--(B);
\draw (B)--(C);
\draw (C)--(D);
\draw (D)--(A) node[midway,left] {$3\text{ cm}$};
\draw (B)--(F)--(G)--(C);
\draw (D)--(H)--(G);
\draw[dashed] (A)--(E)--(F);
\draw[dashed] (E)--(H);
\node[font=\small] at (0.9,-0.55) {$V=7\text{ cm}^3$};
\coordinate (A2) at (3.6,0);
\coordinate (B2) at (5.6,0);
\coordinate (C2) at (5.6,2);
\coordinate (D2) at (3.6,2);
\coordinate (E2) at ($(A2)+(30:1.0)$);
\coordinate (F2) at ($(B2)+(30:1.0)$);
\coordinate (G2) at ($(C2)+(30:1.0)$);
\coordinate (H2) at ($(D2)+(30:1.0)$);
\draw (A2)--(B2);
\draw (B2)--(C2);
\draw (C2)--(D2);
\draw (D2)--(A2) node[midway,left] {$6\text{ cm}$};
\draw (B2)--(F2)--(G2)--(C2);
\draw (D2)--(H2)--(G2);
\draw[dashed] (A2)--(E2)--(F2);
\draw[dashed] (E2)--(H2);
\node at (4.6,1.0) {$V=?$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
